  "caption": "Quinn bought very fancy, very pointy shoes. Two hours later: a pebble feeling under the toes that stayed even with the shoes off.\n\nNarrow, raised shoes can squeeze the forefoot, irritating a nerve between the toes and overloading the ball of the foot. Footwear is usually the first thing to change.\n\nWhat often helps: a wide toe box, lower heel and cushioned sole, a metatarsal pad placed just behind the sore spot, calf stretches and foot strength, and trimming walking while it settles before building back gradually. Very thin minimal shoes aren't always harmless here.\n\nGet it checked if pain sits under one bone, especially at rest or after a jump in walking or running.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
